## Context

0729 and 0814 deferred a causal country comparison. The author has selected a
publishable non-causal comparative measurement paper across South Africa,
Indonesia, Viet Nam and Senegal. This ticket freezes its question before
acquisition or descriptive result inspection.

## First test

Write a protocol validator fixture in which a claimed comparable total mixes a
pledge with a signature, silently turns a missing quarter into zero, or calls a
cross-country gap an effect. The validator must reject all three.

## Actions

Define the study question, unit, countries, evidence cutoff, lifecycle-state
taxonomy, per-state denominators, source universe, inclusion/exclusion rules,
money and date semantics, missingness/lost-visibility vocabulary, and permitted
comparisons. Register prohibited claims: causal acceleration, additionality,
total investment and physical delivery. Retain the 0815 routes as named source
leads, not causal tests. Freeze the protocol and independent review before any
cross-country result table is made.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Immutable study/protocol revision names the four-country scope and every permitted claim
- [ ] Lifecycle states and denominators cannot be mixed in an aggregate or figure
- [ ] Completeness has a finite source-country-period universe and disposition vocabulary
- [ ] Causal language and zero-filled missingness fail the protocol acceptance check
- [ ] Source census handoff for 0817 is frozen before acquisition

